<div class="source-doc-poem">
  <p>We thought it such a sacrilege<br>
  that Grandpa had the privilege<br>
  to lift his tail and thunder left or right<br>
  while his wide eyed little heirs<br>
  had to tiptoe down the stairs<br>
  and softly vent their product in the night</p>

  <p>That's a tuba or a French horn<br>
  loved the sound since I was born<br>
  Reverend Leonard hummed a ditty toward the sky<br>
  but his nostrils started twitchin'<br>
  when he entered Grandma's kitchen<br>
  and our Grandpa let another flatus fly</p>
</div>

